Chapter: IdentLetters
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 An identifier may carry letters from scripts other than English, which is
 what "any language can be used in the source" has to mean at the level of a
 name. The lexer already accepted multi-byte characters through their own
 Tier 1 path; what it refused was the THIRTY-ONE letters that Tier 0 carries
 in one byte, because is-letter's band stopped at 64 and those sit at
 97..127.

Section: Names

  café : Integer = 3

  año : Integer = 4

  дом : Integer = 5

  suma-café-año : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  suma-café-año (a) (b) = a + b

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (suma-café-año café año))
    print-line-uni (show дом)
  end

